s like an exaggerated and  pet achlys will address is that you need  some sort of other cause for explaining  why there is motion or change why did  things go the way that they did we know  that we can take matter and whatever the  matter happens to be it can it can be  take different forms or have different  qualities by configuring it in certain  ways what configures it in that way it's  not going to do it just by itself as  Aristotle says he says um if it is  really true that all generation and  destruction is out of some one entity or  even more than one why does that happen  and what is the cause it's surely not  the substrate at  self which causes itself to change  that's the problem the substrate doesn't  produce its own change or motion so he  says what I mean is that neither wood  nor bronze is responsible for changing  itself Wood does not become a bed nor  bronze a statue but something else is  the cause of the change and we can say  this even with things that are not  human-made artifacts but other types of  bodies that we encounter living beings  for example they they're going to be  affected by something that brings about  the change they may have their  principles of motion to some degree  within themselves but some of it will  also be caused from the outside and we  need to explain that the other thing  that he says that's that's important  here is that these accounts that say  that everything is is one substance or  even just a set of substances they're  kind of implausible and they they seem  rather arbitrary why should it be fire  why should it be water why should it be  this why should it be that this doesn't  provide a full intelligibility to us for  the individual things and the the cosmos  as a whole and that's part of what  metaphysics really ought to supply in  Aristotle's view so these accounts that  are based on material causes whether  they're you know you might say proto  scientific or whether they're  mythological they're really not going to  cut it and the problem is from  Aristotle's perspective they're not  recognizing the importance and the  contribution of the other three causes  you
 

